# Project 2 — Explainability

Project 2 explores machine learning interpretability using the Palmer Penguins dataset.

The objective is to compare predictive performance with model complexity and provide different forms of model explanation.

## Models

Two model types are available:

- Decision Tree
- Logistic Regression

Different levels of regularization are evaluated so that the user can explore the relationship between model complexity and predictive performance.

## Counterfactual Explanations

The interface allows the user to select a penguin and a desired target species.

New samples are generated around the selected example and predictions are evaluated using the currently selected model.

Valid counterfactual examples are ranked using a MAD-weighted L1 distance and the closest examples are displayed to the user.

## Feature Effect Plots

The project also includes:

- Partial Dependence Plots (PDP)
- Accumulated Local Effects (ALE)

These calculations are implemented directly as part of the project rather than using a dedicated explainability package.

The user can select a numerical feature and inspect its effect on the predicted probability of the different penguin species.

## Run

From the repository root:

```bash
python manage.py runserver
```

Then open:

